es differ, give the exact names.\n3) Column H scope: replace formulas with values for the entire column H (including header), or only H from row X to row Y, or H2 through the last data row? Tell me which range to use.\n4) Backup preference (recommended): I will preserve formulas and structure by making a backup copy before any destructive change. Options:\n   - I create a backup sheet named plan_backup_formulas_YYYYMMDD_HHMM (preserves all formulas) and then replace formulas in the active plan sheet; and I either delete the old assumptions tab or move it to a backup named old_assumptions_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMM.\n   - Or I can skip backups and perform the changes directly (this is effectively irreversible).\n   Tell me which you want.\n\nExact actions I will take once you confirm:\n- Step A (non-destructive): Inspect the plan sheet to determine the last row with data in column H and confirm the precise range to change.\n- Step B (backup, reversible): Create a backup copy of the plan sheet that preserves all formulas (name noted above).\n- Step C (destructive unless backed up): Replace formulas in the agreed column H range of the plan sheet with their current evaluated values.\n- Step D (destructive unless backed up): Remove the agreed old assumptions tab (delete or move to backup per your choice).\n\nReversibility:\n- If I create the backup sheet and/or backup the old assumptions tab, the change is reversible by restoring from the backups.\n- If you request no backups and I delete the tab and overwrite formulas, those changes cannot be undone.\n\nDo you want me to wait to run this only after you tell me finance has signed off, or should I run it at a specified date/time? If “wait,” reply with explicit confirmation plus the spreadsheet and the choices above; I will then inspect the sheet and perform the actions after you tell me finance has signed off.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_04e9a1eb19c93be2016a9a6df9717887d0b5e2eb5cd244aa12","role":"assistant","status":"comp